  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Thank you for your continued work on the development and maintenance of VRChat.\n\nI would like to request the addition of a parameter to **control the reflection distance** in `VRCMirrorReflection` — specifically, the maximum distance from which objects are included in the mirror's reflection.\n\nAt the moment, the reflection range cannot be limited by distance, and this can cause several issues depending on how a world is structured:\n\n- In large worlds, distant objects are reflected unnecessarily, which can impact performance\n\n- Unintended far-away objects may appear in the mirror, causing visual inconsistency\n\n- Certain effects that require only nearby objects to be reflected cannot be achieved\n\nHaving the ability to define a reflection distance would improve both performance and creative flexibility, making it easier to design mirrors that fit the intended use case of each world.\n\nI would greatly appreciate your consideration of this feature.\n\nThank you very much.",
